---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import RelatedGuides from '../../components/RelatedGuides.astro';

// BDAE partner links (Orga-Nr. T258845, tracking code M258845)
const BDAE_INFINITY_URL = 'https://oapp.bdae.com/en/agent/expat-infinity-basepricefinder?m=2&mid=M258845';
const BDAE_SMART_URL = 'https://oapp.bdae.com/en/expat-smart-pricefinder?m=2&mid=M258845';
const BDAE_ENTITLEMENT_URL = 'https://oapp.bdae.com/en/entitlement-pricefinder?m=2&mid=M258845';
const BDAE_LIABILITY_URL = 'https://oapp.bdae.com/de/expat-haftpflicht-preisermittlung?m=2&mid=M258845';
const faqSchema = {"@context": "https://schema.org", "@type": "FAQPage", "mainEntity": [{"@type": "Question", "name": "Do I need private health insurance in Greece?", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "Not if you are covered through EFKA as an employee or self-employed person in Greece; your contributions include public health cover. You usually need private insurance for a visa or residence permit, before your Greek registration is complete, or if you want private hospitals and worldwide cover."}}, {"@type": "Question", "name": "Does EFKA include health insurance?", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "Yes. EFKA social security contributions include public health cover through EOPYY, the national health service provider, for you and usually your dependants."}}, {"@type": "Question", "name": "Is private health insurance required for the Greek Digital Nomad Visa?", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "Yes. The Digital Nomad Visa, the financially independent person permit and the Golden Visa all require proof of health insurance that covers you in Greece. Check the exact requirements with your consulate."}}, {"@type": "Question", "name": "Can taxomade recommend a health insurance plan?", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "No. We work with BDAE as a partner, but advice and applications are handled directly by BDAE. We don't compare plans or quote prices."}}]};
---

<Layout title="Health Insurance in Greece for Expats: EFKA vs Private Cover | taxomade" description="Health insurance in Greece for expats: what EFKA covers, when you need private cover (visas, gaps, worldwide protection), liability and accident cover, and our partner BDAE.">
  <main class="pt-32 pb-24 md:pt-40 bg-white">
    <article class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
      <p class="text-sm font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-blue-800 mb-4">Health insurance</p>
      <h1 class="text-4xl md:text-5xl font-black text-slate-900 mb-6 tracking-tight leading-tight">Health insurance in Greece: EFKA vs private cover</h1>
      <p class="text-xl text-slate-600 mb-12 leading-relaxed">
        If you live and work in Greece, health cover usually comes through the public system. Many internationals still need, or want, private insurance on top. Here is how the two fit together.
      </p>

      <div class="prose prose-slate prose-lg max-w-none">
        <h2>EFKA: public cover through your social security</h2>
        <p>
          Once you are registered as self-employed or employed in Greece, you pay social security contributions to EFKA. These contributions include public health cover through EOPYY, the national health service provider. As a freelancer you pay them every month, from the first month of your activity. For how the contribution classes work, see our <a href="/guides/efka-social-security-freelancers-greece/">EFKA guide for freelancers</a>.
        </p>
        <p>
          Public cover gives you access to public hospitals and contracted doctors. Waiting times can be long, and English is not guaranteed. That is why many people add private insurance.
        </p>

        <h2>Who usually needs private cover</h2>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Visa applicants from outside the EU.</strong> The <a href="/greece/digital-nomad-visa/">Digital Nomad Visa</a>, the financially independent person permit and the Golden Visa all require proof of health insurance that covers you in Greece. Check the exact wording your consulate asks for.</li>
          <li><strong>People not (yet) covered through EFKA.</strong> For example remote employees of foreign companies, retirees without an S1 form, or anyone in the months before their Greek registration is complete.</li>
          <li><strong>Anyone who wants more.</strong> Private hospitals, English-speaking doctors, and cover that also applies when you travel or spend time back home.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Our own experience</h2>
        <p>
          We, Manoli and Leonard, have both been insured with BDAE for years, with international health insurance as well as liability and accident insurance. We have also travelled a lot over the past years, and it is good to know we are covered in other countries too. That is our personal experience; what is covered depends on the plan you choose with BDAE.
        </p>
      </div>

      <!-- Partner box -->
      <section class="mt-12 rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 bg-slate-50 p-6 md:p-8">
        <div class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row sm:items-center gap-6">
          <img src="/images/partners/bdae.svg" alt="BDAE logo" class="h-12 w-auto shrink-0" width="188" height="50" loading="lazy" />
          <div>
            <p class="text-lg font-bold text-slate-900 mb-1">Our partner for international health insurance: BDAE</p>
            <p class="text-slate-600">BDAE (Hamburg) specialises in health insurance for people living abroad. Advice and applications are handled directly by BDAE. We don't compare plans, quote prices or help with applications.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="mt-6 grid gap-3 sm:grid-cols-2">
          <a href={BDAE_INFINITY_URL} target="_blank" rel="sponsored noopener" data-cta="bdae-infinity" class="flex flex-col justify-center px-6 py-4 rounded-xl text-white bg-slate-900 hover:bg-blue-800 transition-colors">
            <span class="text-base font-bold">Expat Infinity</span>
            <span class="text-sm text-slate-300">Long-term cover, no time limit</span>
          </a>
          <a href={BDAE_SMART_URL} target="_blank" rel="sponsored noopener" data-cta="bdae-smart" class="flex flex-col justify-center px-6 py-4 rounded-xl text-white bg-slate-900 hover:bg-blue-800 transition-colors">
            <span class="text-base font-bold">Expat Smart</span>
            <span class="text-sm text-slate-300">Cover for up to 5 years</span>
          </a>
        </div>
        <p class="mt-3 text-sm text-slate-600">Which plan fits you is something to clarify directly with BDAE.</p>
        <p class="mt-6 text-xs text-slate-500">We may receive a commission from our partners. This does not affect the price you pay.</p>
      </section>

      <div class="prose prose-slate prose-lg max-w-none mt-12">
        <h2>Other cover worth considering</h2>
        <p>
          Health insurance is the most important one, but it is not the only gap when you move abroad. BDAE also offers:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Prospective entitlement.</strong> If you are not sure yet whether you will stay abroad long term, you can lock in your current state of health and switch to full international cover later without a new health check. Useful, for example, before leaving statutory health insurance in Germany. <a href={BDAE_ENTITLEMENT_URL} target="_blank" rel="sponsored noopener" data-cta="bdae-entitlement">See prospective entitlement</a></li>
          <li><strong>Personal liability insurance.</strong> Covers damage you cause to others, valid worldwide. BDAE's Expat Haftpflicht is available to German citizens. <a href={BDAE_LIABILITY_URL} target="_blank" rel="sponsored noopener" data-cta="bdae-liability">See liability insurance (German)</a></li>
          <li><strong>Accident insurance.</strong> Pays out after an accident that leads to permanent disability, regardless of where in the world it happens. Ask BDAE directly about Expat Accident.</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="text-sm">Advice and applications for all products are handled directly by BDAE.</p>
      </div>

      <section class="mt-12 rounded-2xl border border-emerald-100 bg-emerald-50/60 p-6 md:p-8">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900 mb-3">Health insurance is one part of your setup</h2>
        <p class="text-slate-700 mb-6">Your EFKA registration, tax number and bookkeeping decide how you are covered and what you pay. Not sure your setup is complete? We check it for free.</p>
        <div class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row gap-3">
          <a href="https://wa.me/491743426818?text=Hi%20taxomade%2C%20I%27d%20like%20a%20free%20check%20of%20my%20setup%20in%20Greece." target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-cta="health-insurance-whatsapp" class="inline-flex items-center justify-center px-6 py-3 text-base font-bold rounded-xl text-white bg-emerald-600 hover:bg-emerald-700 transition-colors">Get a free check on WhatsApp</a>
          <a href="/greece/ongoing-bookkeeping/" class="inline-flex items-center justify-center px-6 py-3 text-base font-bold rounded-xl text-slate-700 bg-white border-2 border-slate-200 hover:border-slate-300 transition-colors">See our bookkeeping service</a>
        </div>
      </section>
      <section class="mt-16">
        <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold text-slate-900 mb-8">FAQ</h2>
        <div class="space-y-4">
          <div class="bg-white p-6 rounded-2xl border border-slate-100 shadow-sm">
            <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-slate-900 mb-2">Do I need private health insurance in Greece?</h3>
            <p class="text-slate-700">Not if you are covered through EFKA as an employee or self-employed person in Greece; your contributions include public health cover. You usually need private insurance for a visa or residence permit, before your Greek registration is complete, or if you want private hospitals and worldwide cover.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="bg-white p-6 rounded-2xl border border-slate-100 shadow-sm">
            <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-slate-900 mb-2">Does EFKA include health insurance?</h3>
            <p class="text-slate-700">Yes. EFKA social security contributions include public health cover through EOPYY, the national health service provider, for you and usually your dependants.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="bg-white p-6 rounded-2xl border border-slate-100 shadow-sm">
            <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-slate-900 mb-2">Is private health insurance required for the Greek Digital Nomad Visa?</h3>
            <p class="text-slate-700">Yes. The Digital Nomad Visa, the financially independent person permit and the Golden Visa all require proof of health insurance that covers you in Greece. Check the exact requirements with your consulate.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="bg-white p-6 rounded-2xl border border-slate-100 shadow-sm">
            <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-slate-900 mb-2">Can taxomade recommend a health insurance plan?</h3>
            <p class="text-slate-700">No. We work with BDAE as a partner, but advice and applications are handled directly by BDAE. We don't compare plans or quote prices.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>
    </article>
    <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(faqSchema)}></script>

    <RelatedGuides
      category="tax"
      pinned={["efka-social-security-freelancers-greece", "retiring-to-greece-7-percent-flat-tax", "ultimate-guide-dnv-greece"]}
      title="Further reading"
      subtitle="Social security, visas and retiring in Greece."
    />
  </main>
</Layout>
